#
# LeakSanitizer suppressions for ci/leak-check.sh.
#
# Each entry names a function of GLib or EDS, never a function of this
# project. Give the reason for each entry.

# `e_source_registry_new_sync` builds a real D-Bus client once per process
# and never frees it: a test that reaches the OAuth2 code path holds it in a
# process-wide `Forever` on purpose (see `oauth2.rs`'s `credentials_provider`
# doc), because EDS keeps only a weak reference from the credentials
# provider it feeds. In a sandbox with a session bus, the one-time
# GDBusObjectManagerClient this builds caches its initial properties in a
# way LeakSanitizer cannot trace back to that holder.
leak:e_source_registry_set_default_for_extension_name

# EDS 3.52 computes this directory name once, without a lock. Two threads
# that call it at the same time both allocate the name, and one copy leaks.
# The backend tests construct ESourceServerSide objects in parallel threads.
leak:e_server_side_source_get_user_dir
